          <div class="cog--mq">
      
  <div class="field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__items">
        <div class="field__item"><h2>About Us</h2><p>The Office of Homeless Services leads Nashville's efforts to tackle homelessness.</p><p>As the leads, we tackle homelessness through 5 primary efforts:</p><ul><li>Data Management: Collect and analyze community partners' data entered into the Homeless Management Information System (HMIS)</li><li>Asset Management: Provide oversight to Metro Nashville and Davidson County's Permanent Supportive Housing for our Nashville neighbors exiting homelessness.</li><li>Collaborative Partnerships: Convening government agencies, property managers, community partners, philanthropic and faith-based communities around a common goal to end homelessness in Nashville.</li><li>Grant and Resource Management: Manage federal, state, and local funding opportunities.</li></ul><p>Our Vision is to secure attainable and accessible housing for all Nashvillians.</p><p>Our Mission is to lead Nashville's efforts to end homelessness through innovation, community collaboration and compassion.</p></div>
  </div>
      </div>
      </div>
</div>
  </div>
  </div>


  
